WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
When the price of one
brand of coffee goes up,

2
00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:05.900
plenty of shoppers simply
switch to another brand.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.630
Now imagine every price in
a country goes up at once.

4
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:14.210
Economists still say people would
buy less real output in total.

5
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.360
So if every price in a
country goes up at once,

6
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.260
why would people buy less of its output?

7
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.680
In this mission, you'll build
aggregate demand from households,

8
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.840
firms, government and buyers abroad.

9
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.920
Then you'll use a graph lab to tell a move

10
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.060
along the curve from a
shift of the whole curve.

11
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.520
Your mission: explain why
the curve slopes down,

12
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.680
and what moves it.
